        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "nice, thank you! vim already has this problem, and I even found it easier to reproduce with vim. Some first comments:\r\n1. I can't reproduce the example from the test manually, and if you simulate actual key inputs by changing the last `command` to `feed(:call ...<cr>')`, the test doesn't fail anymore without the fix. I suggest a simpler test (only one final `screen:expect` is necessary: the bottom statusline shows \"Top\" even though the buffer is clearly empty):\r\n```lua\r\n    command('set laststatus=2 statusline=%P | split')\r\n    feed(':put=range(10)<cr>dgg')\r\n```\r\n2. I would expect that it's enough to set `w_redr_status` above in the `FOR_ALL_WINDOWS_IN_TAB(win, curtab)` loop, since statuslines are redrawn anyway when changing to another tab.\r\n3. I'm not sure if the unrelated test still makes sense. Is the statusline really \"stale\" in the first `screen:expect`?\r\n4. Have you checked if there are any related vim/neovim issues?",
