        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "@epithet Thanks for review.\r\n\r\nI simplified the test, I am new to Nvim codebase and was struggling a bit with fixing this in \"right\" place so I put the first `screen:expect` as sanity case for myself. Your proposal is way more elegant and compact.\r\n\r\nAlso agree on moving to `FOR_ALL_WINDOWS_IN_TAB(win, curtab)`. Do you think it should be only set when `xtra != 0` which indeed fixes the issue with `%P` or `%L`, or redraw on any kind of change if buffer is same? I noticed on the terminal test (where I am replacing stale `Top` with correct `All` in expected outcome) that also virtual column (`%V`) in ruler is stale - and that is not related to `xtra` change.\r\n\r\nAs for related issues I only searched Neovim Issues briefly. Will take a better look.",
